feat(kernel): provide the symbols the iOS kexts import but xnu 8796 lacks

The native prelink binds an iOS kext against the kernel's export trie, and the
16.7.16 storage stack imports 42 symbols that xnu-8796.141.3 does not define:
17 C++ members of IOUnifiedAddressTranslator and 25 C functions, mostly the
IOMMU/DART entry points of a driver this port does not run.

vfs_getvfs_with_vfsops() is implemented for real, because APFS uses it.  The rest
are stubs that report themselves once if anything calls them, so a wrong binding
shows up as one line rather than corruption.  All of them are exported through
config/BSDKernel.arm64.exports so the prelink can resolve them by name.
